==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*werpaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*werb-}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{m|ofs|werpa}}, Old Saxon {{m|osx|werpan}}, Old Dutch {{m|odt|werpan}} (Dutch {{m|nl|werpen}}), Old High German {{m|goh|werfan}} (German {{m|de|werfen}}), Old Norse {{m|non|verpa}} (Danish {{m|da|verpe}}), Gothic {{m|got|𐍅𐌰𐌹𐍂𐍀𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root also led to Latin {{m|la|verbera}}, Russian {{m|ru|верба}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈweorpan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[throw]], cast down, [[warp]]

